            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susie Gute Wall"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled it and fit it into a 13X9 pan. I used 10 small/medium apples because I didn't want to do the work of pealing so I just used an apple slicer/corer to make it SUPER EASY and fast. \nI cooked it for 1 hour. It was crunchy and stayed crunchy the next day but I understand what others say about it being mushy. The kids and everyone still loved it. I will for sure do it again because the family loved it and it was fast and easy.",
            "datePublished": "2016-09-19T16:14:55.703Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mina Kerr"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used just 1 cup of brown sugar and probably more apples. I cut them pretty thick so they wouldn't get mushy and piled them into a 10 inch pie plate. I baked it one hour so it got nice and crunchy. Really good the next day too! Best with ice cream! Very easy. I blended the cold butter and the flour/br sugar mixture with my fingers because I didn't have any kitchen tools!",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-30T18:08:47.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
